NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: Largely NAMING/application, not a new caching mechanism. The eviction MECHANISM (protected floor + priority/class-ordered eviction over prefix blocks) is pre-existing (TRT-LLM retention priority, SGLang refcount+LRU, CachedAttention scheduler). The genuinely-distinct piece is the SEMANTIC CLASSIFIER — labeling one-shot TOOL-RESULT payloads COMMITTED-vs-TRANSIENT to set eviction order. But the demonstrated benefit reduces to classical scan-resistant caching (evict one-touch data first), re-applied to LLM tool outputs. So the delta over prior work is "use a tool-call-boundary signal to detect one-touch KV blocks," i.e. a domain-specific hint feeding a known mechanism — an application contribution, not a mechanism contribution. That can still be publishable, but it must be FRAMED honestly as such, not as a novel cache policy.

